{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-010", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": -0.17, "keywords": ["growth", "slow", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam manufacturing growth slows in Sept as export orders weaken", "content": "Vietnam’s manufacturing PMI fell to 51.9 in September from 53.3 in August, staying above the 50 growth line for a fifteenth month. \nOutput and new orders still rose, but export demand fell for a second month and at the sharpest pace since April. \nFor sourcing teams, higher fuel, oil and transport costs, longer delivery times and lower finished-goods stocks point to tighter planning needs. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-manufacturing-growth-slows-in-sept-as-export-orders-weaken-313973-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-011", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "China’s Bangladesh push goes upstream: Who gains the fabric edge?", "content": "Chinese textile investment in Bangladesh is moving beyond garment assembly into fabric, yarn, automation and integrated manufacturing.\nTexPro shows selected Chinese knitted and woven fabric exports to Bangladesh rose 4.63 per cent to about $4.18 billion in January to August 2026.\nThe test is whether new Chinese-backed plants cut cross-border fabric flows once commercial production starts.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/china-s-bangladesh-push-goes-upstream-who-gains-the-fabric-edge--313975-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "nike-2026-10-05-012", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": ["nike"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["growth", "excess inventory"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Nike shares tumble: China slump, Q1 miss and the pace reset plan", "content": "Q1 FY2027 revenue was $11.21 billion, $106 million below Wall Street expectations, and Nike guided for a high single-digit fall this fiscal year.\nGreater China fell 26 per cent and EMEA 5 per cent, with Sportswear and Jordan declining amid promotions and excess inventory.\nPace restructuring, a China digital reset and performance growth are key fixes; savings are seen at about $2.5 billion.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/nike-shares-tumble-china-slump-q1-miss-and-the-pace-reset-plan-313976-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-013", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India, Switzerland expand trade ties, sign mobility agreements", "content": "India and Switzerland agreed in New Delhi to widen market access for Indian exports, including textiles, after Modi-Parmelin talks. \nNew pacts on migration, young professionals and transport aim to support trade, investment and trusted supply chains. \nModi linked the push to the India-EFTA TEPA, implemented in October last year, targeting $100 billion investment and 1 million direct jobs. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-switzerland-expand-trade-ties-sign-mobility-agreements-313968-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-014", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India & Canada to begin 5-day CEPA negotiation round in Ottawa today", "content": "India and Canada are set to begin their 5th CEPA negotiation round in Ottawa today, running until Oct 9, with both seeking to conclude talks by year-end. \nThe proposed agreement could reduce tariffs and address investment and skilled-professional mobility.\nDiscussions also focused on energy, critical minerals, and supporting bilateral goal of raising trade to C$70 billion (~$48.95 billion) annually by 2030.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-canada-to-begin-5-day-cepa-negotiation-round-in-ottawa-today-313965-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-015", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["weak", "[否定]uncertainty"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "North Indian cotton yarn stable, sentiment remains weak", "content": "Cotton yarn prices remained steady in Ludhiana and Delhi, but weak sentiment, volatile ICE cotton and tight payment flows kept buyers cautious.\nPanipat’s recycled yarn market stayed subdued despite some festival demand, with home textile exports limited by global geopolitical uncertainty.\nNorth Indian cotton prices held steady as mills bought new-crop cotton only for immediate needs.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/north-indian-cotton-yarn-stable-sentiment-remains-weak-313964-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-016", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Mixed trend continues in India's key polyester raw materials", "content": "Indian polyester raw materials opened October mixed: MEG fell ₹5 (~$0.05) per kg, PTA stayed at ₹106.50, (~$1.10), and polyester melt was cut ₹1.70 (~$0.02).\nPSF and polyester filament yarn were rolled over after September hikes, limiting relief for spinners, mills and sourcing teams.\nViscose and lyocell fibre became costlier, while Asian PTA and MEG weakened before China’s Golden Week closure.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/mixed-trend-continues-in-india-s-key-polyester-raw-materials-313963-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-017", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "India-US trade talks hit ‘plateau’ as concessions narrow: Sitharaman", "content": "India-US trade talks have reached a “plateau”, with Indian Finance Minister Nirmala Sitharaman saying both sides have little room left for further concessions. \nHowever, negotiations remain ongoing as the two countries work to resolve key sticking points and conclude an interim bilateral trade agreement after months of discussions. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-us-trade-talks-hit-plateau-as-concessions-narrow-sitharaman-313962-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-10-05-018", "date": "2026-10-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh’s apparel industry and the changing fabric equation", "content": "Bangladesh exported an estimated $38.825 billion worth of apparel in 2025, but 76.94 per cent of its export basket came from basic categories.\nA September 2026 amendment to the Import Policy Order 2026–2029 has eased access to specialised fabrics for specified apparel categories.\nThe change could support sportswear, functional apparel, MMF-based products and wider product diversification.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/bangladesh-s-apparel-industry-and-the-changing-fabric-equation-313911-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
